      "review": "Device-info uses a 14-byte prefix and two bytes per associated route. Network-info uses exactly 24 bytes: uint16 address, uint8 state, uint16 PAN, uint16 parent, eight-byte extended PAN, eight-byte parent IEEE, uint8 channel. The document grid omits device state and incorrectly describes a two-byte channel. The finite profile follows the exact Z-Stack source, not neighboring TI 15.4-stack files in the same SDK. No SDK source is redistributed."
